  {/* ===== Trust ===== */}
  <section id="trust" class="panel">
    <div class="reveal section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Security posture</p>
      <h2 class="display-lg text-fg">Built for procurement reviews.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 text-sm reveal-group cards-hover">
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">release integrity</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">Sigstore Cosign keyless signing with attested build provenance. Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived registry tokens.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">sbom</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">CycloneDX SBOM published with every release, verifiable from GitHub release artifacts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">vuln scanning</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">gitleaks and a high-severity dependency audit on every push; cargo-deny in the pre-push gate; OSV-Scanner, Grype and cargo-deny nightly and a Syft SBOM weekly on the public repository.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">pre-flight policy</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">Policy checks run inline at the gateway before the call leaves. Today: schema-violation + tool-definition-drift on the Anthropic Messages route, fail-open. More on a published roadmap.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">transport</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">TLS 1.3 from the edge to the origin and on the internal ingest leg, which is mTLS via SPIFFE/SPIRE; the public edge accepts TLS 1.2. SSRF defense — RFC1918, link-local and CGNAT denied.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-6">
        <p class="card-index">standards</p>
        <p class="card-body text-sm">OTel GenAI semconv — tracking the pre-execution judgment / negative-proof proposal (<a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/issues/3244" class="link-accent" rel="noopener">#3244</a>).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== FAQ ===== */}
  <section id="faq" class="panel">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,20rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">FAQ</p>
        <h2 class="display-lg text-fg">Frequently asked.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">What is Tracelane?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">An open-source (Apache 2.0) flight recorder for AI agents: a universal Rust LLM gateway, full-fidelity OpenTelemetry observability, and a tamper-evident audit ledger. Each ledger event is SHA-256 hash-chained and, every 100 events per tenant, the Merkle root is Ed25519-signed, so any gateway call's record can be verified offline. OTLP/SDK traces are not yet in the chain.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">How is it different from Helicone, LangSmith or Langfuse?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Tracelane unifies the gateway, observability, pre-flight policy and a tamper-evident audit ledger in one stack: a Rust gateway and a Rust ingest service. Licensing: Tracelane is Apache 2.0 core with a published self-host path; Helicone's AI gateway is GPL-3.0, Arize Phoenix is ELv2 (no SaaS resale), LangSmith is closed-source. Langfuse has no gateway; Helicone and LangSmith ship theirs separately from their observability products. The audit ledger is hash-chained and Ed25519-signed.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">What about LangSmith Engine?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">LangSmith Engine (announced May 2026) clusters production failures after they happen and drafts pull requests to fix them, inside the LangSmith trace surface; Tracelane's pre-flight policy checks flag failure modes at the gateway and its ingest is neutral OTel with 0% BYOK markup across 191 providers. Different layer of the agent reliability stack.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">Is Tracelane really open source?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes. The core (Rust gateway, ingest workers, observability backend, pre-flight layer, CLI, SDKs, audit verifiers) is Apache 2.0. The AFT-1 spec under <code class="font-mono text-sm">/spec/aft-1</code> is CC0. Paid features are gated by the workspace_entitlements table at the application layer, not by a license-string compare.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">Which providers are supported?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">191 providers today — 6 native adapters (Anthropic, Google Gemini, Google Vertex, AWS Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Cohere) plus 185 catalogued OpenAI-compatible providers including OpenAI, Together, Fireworks, Groq, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, xAI and Mistral; self-hosters can point any catalog entry at their own base URL. One canonical wire format across all of them.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">Does Tracelane support EU AI Act Article 12?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">The Tamper-Evident Agent Ledger (SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed Merkle root, Rekor anchoring, self-verification) is included on every tier, free and paid — no add-on to buy. Enterprise includes a seven-year ledger window and the ledger export (/v1/audit/export); the Article 12 evidence pack — per-record inclusion proofs and a signed completeness attestation — is on the roadmap. Tracelane enforces no per-tenant storage region, signs no BAA, and makes no regulatory-conformance claim. EU AI Act Annex III obligations were originally scheduled for Aug 2, 2026; the Digital Omnibus political agreement (May 7, 2026) provisionally deferred enforcement to Dec 2, 2027, pending formal adoption (<a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" class="link-accent" rel="noopener">details</a>). The ledger ships now so regulated buyers can build audit history before binding enforcement.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">What's the latency overhead?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Measured, not targeted: <strong>2ms p50, 4ms p95, 5ms p99</strong> of added latency (excluding provider time), taken with LiteLLM's open AIGatewayBench harness on a 4 vCPU host with capture on, two runs, alongside Bifrost, Portkey and LiteLLM — see the <a class="underline" href="#benchmarks">full breakdown above</a> or the <a class="underline" href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/benchmarks">benchmark page</a> for method, caveats and the raw CSVs. The pre-flight policy layer is still an engineering target (p99 &lt;50ms on commodity CPU).</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">Can I self-host?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes. One Docker Compose file (infra/self-host/docker-compose.yml) runs the gateway, ingest, NATS and ClickHouse; a Helm chart is on the roadmap. Tracelane's own production — ClickHouse with an R2 cold tier — runs on one Hetzner node. The self-host Compose runs ClickHouse on local disk; an S3/R2 cold tier is a by-hand step. See the <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/self-hosting" class="link-accent" rel="noopener">self-hosting guide</a>.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-row">
          <summary class="text-fg">Is Tracelane available now?<span class="sign" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
          <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes — V1 is live. Start free at <a href="https://app.tracelane.dev/sign-in" class="link-accent">app.tracelane.dev</a>, or self-host the Apache 2.0 core.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

